@* The ways through configuration, folded behind one disclosure in the page, never a dialog: the operator named by
   Tangent:Operator in place of the setup code, where the page asks for one, and the base URL set by its key, where
   the page shows it. Each is one sentence; each takes a restart. *@
<details class="first-run-configuration">
    <summary>Set it in configuration instead</summary>
    <ul>
        @if (AsksCode)
        {
            <li>Set <code>@FirstRun.OperatorSetting</code> to your DID and restart, and no setup code is asked.</li>
        }
        @if (Setting is { } setting)
        {
            <li>Set <code>@setting</code> in appsettings.json, or <code>@setting.Replace(":", "__")</code> in the environment, and restart to answer elsewhere.</li>
        }
    </ul>
</details>

@code {
    /// <summary>The key the base URL is read from, where the page shows the base URL.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Setting { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether the page asks for the setup code, which naming the operator in configuration replaces.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool AsksCode { get; set; }
}
